      "event_type": "ask",
      "field": null,
      "value": {
        "body": "Mine keeps dropping with a 1006 (abnormal close, no close frame) at a variable ~1–4 min — sometimes 70s, sometimes 3 min. I don't think it's my app: I disabled the server's WS keepalive pings, and I attached over the DevTools protocol and confirmed the socket's bufferedAmount stays 0 the whole time (no backpressure in either direction — client and server both healthy). A bare low-traffic probe survived 4 min, but a real streaming connection dies earlier.\n\nIt really looks like the gateway is abruptly killing long-lived connections. Is that expected? Is there any way to configure the WS idle/max-lifetime timeout on the gateway — or is the recommended pattern to avoid long-lived sockets entirely (chunked HTTP / reconnect)?",
